* FRI and proximity proofs\nby theme
** Codes and distance
*** Hamming weight\n//count of non-zero coordinates//
*** Relative Hamming distance\n//fraction of differing coordinates//
*** Linear code\n//subspace with parameters n, k, l//
*** Codeword\n//element of the code, an encoded message//
*** Minimum distance\n//smallest gap between two codewords//
*** Singleton bound and MDS code\n//k at most n - l + 1, tight for MDS//
** Reed-Solomon setting
*** Finite field\n//integers modulo a prime p//
*** Evaluation domain\n//the n points where polynomials are evaluated//
*** Rate\n//message length over codeword length//
*** Reed-Solomon code\n//evaluation tables of low-degree polynomials//
** Decoding radii
*** Unique decoding distance\n//half the minimum distance, one codeword//
*** List decoding\n//all codewords within radius delta//
*** Johnson bound\n//1 - sqrt(rho), list provably bounded//
*** Delta-close and delta-far\n//within delta of the code, or beyond it//
left side
** Proof models
*** Prover and verifier\n//the two parties of a proof system//
*** Interactive oracle proof (IOP)\n//strings sent, cells read after challenges//
*** Soundness, knowledge soundness and succinctness\n//what an IOP must guarantee//
** Commitments and compilation
*** Committed string (oracle access)\n//fixed string read cell by cell//
*** BCS compiler\n//Merkle roots plus Fiat-Shamir give a SNARK//
*** Fiat-Shamir transformation\n//challenges from a hash of the transcript//
*** Virtual oracle\n//derived string computed from committed cells//
** Evaluation proofs
*** Polynomial IOP (Poly-IOP)\n//messages are bounded-degree polynomials//
*** Quotienting\n//(u - b) / (x - a) tests a claimed value//
*** Vanishing and interpolation polynomials\n//quotient by several points at once//
*** DEEP (out-of-domain sampling)\n//random (r, s) pins one polynomial//
** Proximity testing
*** IOP of proximity (IOPP)\n//soundness only against delta-far inputs//
*** Reed-Solomon IOPP\n//is the committed word close to the code//
*** Distance-preserving transformation\n//far inputs give a far output//
*** Proximity gap theorem (BCIKS)\n//combinations close for no r or every r//
*** Folding\n//even and odd split, degree and domain halve//
@endmindmap
